# Copy to .env.local for local development. Never commit .env.local.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are compiled into the browser bundle, so they must be
# safe to publish. API_PROXY_TARGET is read on the server only and is not a
# secret either. The one secret here is WEB_PROXY_SECRET (below); every
# other secret lives in flyviman-api.

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/api/v1

# Hosted with the API on an unrelated domain (D-065): proxy /api/v1 through
# this site so session cookies stay on one origin. Then set
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://<this site>/api/v1
#   API_PROXY_TARGET=https://<the API's own address>   (no /api/v1, no slash)
# API_PROXY_TARGET=
#
# Optional, with API_PROXY_TARGET: the same value as the API's
# WEB_PROXY_SECRET, at least 32 characters (openssl rand -base64 48). This
# site then signs each visitor's address with it, so the API's rate limits
# and sign-in lockout count visitors apart. Unset, /api/v1 is proxied as
# before and every visitor counts as this host's address.
# The visitor's address is read from x-real-ip, which Vercel sets; another
# host must overwrite that header itself. Server only; never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# WEB_PROXY_SECRET=
#
# Nothing is signed unless this host overwrites x-real-ip with the visitor's
# own address: automatic on Vercel (VERCEL=1); elsewhere set TRUST_REAL_IP=1
# only where the platform does so (D-123). Server only, not a secret.
# TRUST_REAL_IP=

# Emergency switch: 1 sends the Content-Security-Policy as report-only, so a
# policy that blocks something it should not only logs in the browser console
# (src/lib/csp.ts). Leave unset: the policy is enforced. Read at build time,
# so a change needs a rebuild (a redeploy on Vercel).
# CSP_REPORT_ONLY=

# Payments (M9). The API names the gateway and its public key with each
# order, so the site needs no key of its own. With the API's mock gateway, the
# test checkout ("Pay (test)", "Fail (test)") shows in development by itself;
# 1 shows it in a production build too, for the browser tests only. Never set
# it in a deployment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_CHECKOUT=

# Business details the client supplies later. Unset means "not shown" (or the
# built-in default for the contact details). An invalid value is ignored with
# a server warning. See src/lib/site-settings.ts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=919779920011       digits with country code
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_INSTAGRAM=https://www.instagram.com/<profile>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_FACEBOOK=https://www.facebook.com/<profile>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_YOUTUBE=https://www.youtube.com/@<channel>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_X=https://x.com/<profile>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_LINKEDIN=https://www.linkedin.com/company/<profile>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LOGO_PATH=/logo.svg                a file under public/
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=info@flyviman.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_PHONES=+91 97799 20011,+91 84471 73787
